    LLM: 'Keep tiles that preserve several matching ends for your own train, and play high pip tiles when they do not damage your future options.\n\nAfter extending your own train, use optional plays on opponents’ trains to reduce pip risk while avoiding openings that help the leader empty quickly.\n\nTrack which numbers each opponent can or cannot extend. Since there is no draw pile, blocking information is strong and endgame pip control matters.',
